---
source: crates/rupu-agentiflow/tests/it/flow_toolset_parity.rs
expression: "lead_toolset(\"[]\")"
---
- description: "Get one agent's detail by name: description, provider, model, declared tools, the agents it may dispatch, and its permission mode."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      name:
        description: "The agent's name, as agents.list shows it"
        type: string
    required:
      - name
    type: object
  name: agents.get
- description: "List the agents you can draw on (global and project): each one's name, description and declared tools. `tools: null` means the agent uses the default tool set, not none. Use agents.get for one agent's detail."
  input_schema:
    properties: {}
    type: object
  name: agents.list
- description: "Record how deeply an engagement asset has been examined, as a rung of its profile's coverage depth ladder (monotonic — a shallower rung after a deeper one keeps the deeper one). The effective rung is returned."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      coordinates:
        description: "Locator coordinates pinning the asset, each {\"t\": <tag>, \"v\": <value>}."
        items:
          type: object
        type: array
      depth:
        description: "The depth-ladder rung reached, e.g. \"tested\"."
        type: string
      kind:
        description: "Profile-namespaced asset kind, e.g. \"network:service\"."
        type: string
      label:
        type: string
    required:
      - kind
      - depth
    type: object
  name: assets.mark
- description: "Atomically claim a work unit so no other participant duplicates it. Returns granted, or the current holder when it is already claimed."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      work_unit:
        description: "Identifier of the unit of work to claim, e.g. host:1.1.2.2"
        type: string
    required:
      - work_unit
    type: object
  name: board.claim
- description: "Steer the fleet: write a standing directive to the board. Units see it on every turn until you lift it, so post sparingly and keep each short and actionable. Returns the directive's `id`: pass it to `board.retract` once the instruction is obsolete. Omit `addressed_to` to address everyone; name a unit or role to address only it."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      addressed_to:
        description: "A participant (lynx#1), role:<agent> or step:<id> to address; omit for everyone"
        type: string
      body:
        description: The directive text
        type: string
    required:
      - body
    type: object
  name: board.directive
- description: "Post to the shared board every participant can read: an observation, a question, an answer, a vote, or a note. Optionally address it to a participant (lynx#1), role:<agent>, step:<id>, parent or lead. Returns the post's `id` and who it was resolved to."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      addressed_to:
        description: "Who this post is for: a participant (lynx#1), role:<agent>, step:<id>, parent or lead; omit for everyone"
        type: string
      body:
        type: string
      kind:
        enum:
          - observation
          - question
          - answer
          - vote
          - note
        type: string
    required:
      - kind
      - body
    type: object
  name: board.post
- description: "Read the shared board's posts, oldest first, newest last. Returns the most recent posts (default 50); filter to those addressed to a participant id or role with addressed_to."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      addressed_to:
        description: Only posts addressed to this participant id or role
        type: string
      limit:
        description: Maximum posts to return (the most recent ones); default 50
        maximum: 500
        minimum: 1
        type: integer
    type: object
  name: board.read
- description: "Release a work unit you previously claimed with board.claim, so another participant can take it."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      work_unit:
        description: Identifier of the claimed unit of work to release
        type: string
    required:
      - work_unit
    type: object
  name: board.release
- description: "Lift a standing directive: pass the `id` that `board.directive` returned (it is also shown in brackets on each standing directive you see each turn). Units stop seeing it from their next turn. An unknown or already retracted id is reported and changes nothing."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      id:
        description: "The `id` `board.directive` returned for the directive to lift"
        type: string
    required:
      - id
    type: object
  name: board.retract
- description: "Re-check the run's budget against what it has spent right now: the lead's own and every unit's usage so far, read fresh. `stage` is `ok`, `soft` (a dimension crossed its soft threshold: converge) or `hard` (a cap is reached and the run stops at the next round check; `tripped` names the dimension). Each dimension the flow sets is reported with its `cap`, what it has used (`spent` for `usd` / `tokens`, `elapsed` rounds completed before this one or `elapsed_secs` for `wall_clock`), what is `remaining` and its own `state`. A `usd` cap nothing can price carries `enforced: false` and a note. `{budget: null}` when the flow sets no budget."
  input_schema:
    properties: {}
    type: object
  name: budget.status
- description: "Search the agent and workflow catalog: a case-insensitive substring match over agent name/description and workflow id/name/description. Each hit is tagged kind=agent|workflow. `warnings` is present when part of the catalog could not be read."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      query:
        description: Substring to look for (case-insensitive)
        type: string
    required:
      - query
    type: object
  name: catalog.search
- description: "Start a child run and get a handle back at once; the child works on its own. `kind` picks how it runs: `subagent` (the default: in this process, for a quick delegation such as reviewing a file), `agent` (its own `rupu run` process, for long or heavy work), or `workflow` (its own `rupu workflow run`). Name an agent from your dispatchable agents, a workflow from your dispatchable workflows, or pass a `file` that `workflows.generate` returned. Call `join` with the handle to collect the result, or pass `wait: true` to start the child and wait for it in one call. Children you never join are stopped when you finish."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      file:
        description: "Kind `workflow` only: a workflow file `workflows.generate` returned, instead of `name`"
        type: string
      inputs:
        additionalProperties: true
        description: "A workflow's declared inputs as name: value pairs; for an agent, structured inputs added to its prompt"
        type: object
      kind:
        description: "How the child runs; default `subagent`"
        enum:
          - subagent
          - agent
          - workflow
        type: string
      name:
        description: "The agent (or, for kind `workflow`, the workflow) to run"
        type: string
      prompt:
        description: "An agent child's task: what to do and what to report back"
        type: string
      timeout_secs:
        description: "With `wait`: how long to wait, in seconds; default 300"
        maximum: 3600
        minimum: 0
        type: integer
      wait:
        description: Wait for the child to finish and return its result too; default false
        type: boolean
    type: object
  name: dispatch
- description: "Record a security or quality finding in this project's ledger. Returns the generated finding id (use it in coverage.mark calls and in another finding's cross_references). Under the full profile send a complete `report`; a rejected call lists every problem to fix."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      asset:
        description: "The engagement asset this finding is about (only under an active engagement profile). Its `kind` routes the finding to the owning profile for completeness validation and stamps it into the asset graph. Omit on a plain code run."
        properties:
          coordinates:
            description: "Locator coordinates pinning the asset, each {\"t\": <tag>, \"v\": <value>}. Tags: host, port, url, path, line_range, symbol, sha256, address, offset, commit, http_route, param, resource_id."
            items:
              type: object
            type: array
          kind:
            description: "Profile-namespaced asset kind, e.g. \"network:service\", \"binary:function\", \"web:route\"."
            type: string
          label:
            description: "Optional human label; if omitted, the asset keeps its existing label (a new asset is labelled with its kind)."
            type: string
        required:
          - kind
        type: object
      concern_id:
        description: "Concern ID this finding relates to, if known."
        type: string
      file_path:
        description: "Workspace-relative path of the affected file, if applicable."
        type: string
      line_range:
        description: "Line range [start, end] within the file, if applicable."
        items:
          type: integer
        maxItems: 2
        minItems: 2
        type: array
      report:
        description: "A complete security finding report, recorded once by the agent. Presentations and exports (Markdown, HTML, PDF) are generated from this report, so no separate report file is written. When information genuinely cannot be determined use the field's sentinel instead of omitting it: 'Unknown', 'Not Applicable', 'None Provided', 'None', or 'Not Provided — <justification>' as each field describes."
        properties:
          artifacts:
            description: "Proof-of-concept files (scripts, outputs, harnesses) as workspace-relative paths; rupu stores them with the finding. Supply only 'path'."
            items:
              properties:
                path:
                  type: string
              required:
                - path
              type: object
            type: array
          attack_vector:
            description: "How the surface is reached, including authentication or user interaction required, or 'Unknown'."
            type: string
          blocks:
            description: "Typed evidence blocks (engagement profiles): each an object with a 'kind' tag and that kind's fields, e.g. {\"kind\":\"scan_output\",\"tool\":\"nmap\",\"output\":\"...\"} or {\"kind\":\"http_exchange\",\"request\":\"...\",\"response\":\"...\"}. Optional; additive to 'evidence'."
            items:
              properties:
                kind:
                  enum:
                    - text
                    - code_slice
                    - diff
                    - table
                    - image
                    - hexdump
                    - disasm
                    - decompile
                    - http_exchange
                    - scan_output
                    - pcap_ref
                  type: string
              required:
                - kind
              type: object
            type: array
          call_chain:
            anyOf:
              - items:
                  properties:
                    binary_va:
                      description: binary@VA for binary-only targets.
                      type: string
                    file:
                      description: Workspace-relative path.
                      type: string
                    gate:
                      description: Precondition crossed at this hop.
                      type: string
                    label:
                      description: Function or surface name.
                      type: string
                    lines:
                      items:
                        type: integer
                      maxItems: 2
                      minItems: 2
                      type: array
                    passes_because:
                      description: Why the gate passes.
                      type: string
                    role:
                      enum:
                        - source
                        - hop
                        - sink
                      type: string
                  required:
                    - label
                    - role
                  type: object
                minItems: 1
                type: array
              - type: string
            description: "Ordered path from the externally reachable entry point to the sink, or 'Not Provided — <justification>'."
          category:
            type: string
          ci_cd_detection:
            anyOf:
              - properties:
                  body:
                    description: "Markdown. The rule or test, verbatim."
                    type: string
                  command:
                    type: string
                  expect:
                    description: The failing signal.
                    type: string
                  stage:
                    description: pre-merge / nightly / release gate.
                    type: string
                required:
                  - stage
                  - body
                  - expect
                type: object
              - type: string
            description: "A pipeline check that fails the build when this class of issue is present, or 'Not Provided — <justification>'."
          classifications:
            description: "Classifications across taxonomies (engagement profiles), e.g. {\"system\":\"CVE\",\"id\":\"CVE-2024-1234\"} or {\"system\":\"ATT&CK\",\"id\":\"T1190\"}. Optional; additive to 'cwe'."
            items:
              properties:
                id:
                  type: string
                system:
                  type: string
                vector:
                  type: string
              required:
                - system
                - id
              type: object
            type: array
          cross_references:
            anyOf:
              - enum:
                  - None
                type: string
              - items:
                  properties:
                    finding_id:
                      type: string
                    note:
                      type: string
                    relation:
                      enum:
                        - duplicate
                        - sibling
                        - prerequisite
                        - supersedes
                      type: string
                  required:
                    - finding_id
                    - relation
                  type: object
                minItems: 1
                type: array
            description: "'None', or related findings by the fnd_ id a previous report_finding call returned."
          cwe:
            description: "CWE ids, e.g. ['CWE-306']. May be empty."
            items:
              type: string
            type: array
          description:
            description: "Markdown. What the issue is, where it occurs, why it is a weakness."
            type: string
          evidence:
            description: "Minimal annotated proof, one claim per entry."
            items:
              properties:
                artifact:
                  description: Path of an entry in artifacts that proves this claim.
                  type: string
                binary_va:
                  type: string
                claim:
                  type: string
                excerpt:
                  description: Only the lines that matter.
                  type: string
                file:
                  description: Workspace-relative path.
                  type: string
                lang:
                  description: "Language for highlighting, e.g. 'c', 'sh'."
                  type: string
                lines:
                  items:
                    type: integer
                  maxItems: 2
                  minItems: 2
                  type: array
              required:
                - claim
              type: object
            minItems: 1
            type: array
          impact:
            description: Markdown. What an attacker could achieve and why it matters.
            type: string
          location:
            properties:
              input:
                description: "Markdown. Input surface, endpoint, parameter, or feature."
                type: string
              output:
                description: "Markdown. Affected area, response, or downstream system."
                type: string
            required:
              - input
              - output
            type: object
          ownership:
            properties:
              affected_component:
                description: "Exact feature/endpoint/module, or 'Unknown'."
                type: string
              owner:
                description: "Accountable team/service owner, or 'Unknown'. Never invent one."
                type: string
              product:
                description: "Named application/platform/service, or 'Unknown'."
                type: string
              source_repository:
                description: "Canonical repository (optionally with a path), 'Not Applicable' when no source-controlled code is involved, or 'Unknown'."
                type: string
            required:
              - owner
              - product
              - affected_component
              - source_repository
            type: object
          rating:
            properties:
              cvss_v3:
                description: "Base score, optionally with the vector string, or 'Unknown'. Never invent a score."
                type: string
              impact:
                enum:
                  - Low
                  - Medium
                  - High
                  - Critical
                type: string
              likelihood:
                enum:
                  - Low
                  - Medium
                  - High
                type: string
              risk_factor:
                enum:
                  - Low
                  - Medium
                  - High
                  - Critical
                type: string
              risk_rating:
                description: "Drives the finding's severity."
                enum:
                  - Low
                  - Medium
                  - High
                  - Critical
                type: string
            required:
              - impact
              - likelihood
              - risk_rating
              - risk_factor
              - cvss_v3
            type: object
          recommended_patch:
            anyOf:
              - properties:
                  diff:
                    type: string
                  notes:
                    description: Markdown. Alternatives or the equivalent source-level change.
                    type: string
                required:
                  - diff
                type: object
              - type: string
            description: "Minimal unified diff against the source repository (or a binary@VA pseudo-diff), or 'Not Provided — <justification>'."
          references:
            description: "Markdown. CWE, OWASP category, control references, related tickets."
            type: string
          regression_test:
            anyOf:
              - properties:
                  body:
                    type: string
                  command:
                    type: string
                  expect_patched:
                    type: string
                  expect_vulnerable:
                    type: string
                required:
                  - body
                  - command
                  - expect_vulnerable
                  - expect_patched
                type: object
              - type: string
            description: "A deterministic test that fails on the vulnerable build and passes on the patched one, or 'Not Provided — <justification>'."
          remediation:
            description: Markdown. Specific corrective actions.
            type: string
          replication_steps:
            description: "Sequential, reproducible steps with exact payloads and commands."
            items:
              type: string
            minItems: 1
            type: array
          root_cause:
            description: "Markdown, one or two sentences. The single underlying defect, naming the exact variable, check, or assumption that is wrong — not the symptom."
            type: string
          tickets:
            anyOf:
              - enum:
                  - None Provided
                  - Unknown
                type: string
              - items:
                  properties:
                    identifier:
                      type: string
                    notes:
                      type: string
                    type:
                      description: Jira / Bug / Remediation Tracker / Vulnerability Management / Other.
                      type: string
                    url:
                      type: string
                  required:
                    - type
                    - identifier
                  type: object
                minItems: 1
                type: array
            description: "'None Provided' when no existing ticket is mentioned, 'Unknown' when one exists but its id is not given, or the tickets present in the evidence. Never invent a ticket."
          title:
            description: Short title specific to the vulnerable feature and target.
            type: string
        required:
          - title
          - ownership
          - tickets
          - rating
          - category
          - attack_vector
          - cwe
          - description
          - impact
          - location
          - root_cause
          - call_chain
          - evidence
          - remediation
          - recommended_patch
          - ci_cd_detection
          - regression_test
          - replication_steps
          - cross_references
          - references
        title: rupu finding report
        type: object
      scope:
        description: "What the finding is about. Code scopes: 'line' (needs file_path + line_range), 'file' (needs file_path), 'repo' (the project as a whole). Target scopes, each needing target_ref: 'host' (a machine or IP), 'endpoint' (a specific service URL), 'resource' (a cloud resource by its own id). Pick the narrowest scope the evidence actually supports - claiming a whole host for a defect on one endpoint overstates it."
        enum:
          - line
          - file
          - repo
          - host
          - endpoint
          - resource
        type: string
      tags:
        description: "Free-form tags: lowercase a-z, 0-9 and . _ : / -, starting with a letter or digit, e.g. class:sqli, needs-poc. Reuse tags already in use where they fit (findings.query lists them)."
        items:
          type: string
        maxItems: 32
        type: array
      target_ref:
        description: "What this finding is about when it is not a file: a host or IP (host), a URL (endpoint), or a cloud resource id such as an OCID/ARN/URN (resource). Required for those three scopes."
        type: string
    required:
      - scope
      - report
    type: object
  name: findings.report
- description: "Re-check the engagement coverage target against the pooled assets right now. `reach` is the required fraction and `depth` the rung assets must have reached (null: the ladder's terminal rung); `fraction` is what has been reached so far, `satisfied` whether it meets `reach`, `per_kind` the per-asset-kind fractions. `{coverage: null}` when the flow sets no coverage target."
  input_schema:
    properties: {}
    type: object
  name: goal.coverage
- description: "Re-check every goal against the pooled evidence right now (findings and assets banked since the round began count). Each goal reports `satisfied`, its `current`/`target` tally and a one-line `detail`; a goal that could not be evaluated carries an `error` instead. A findings goal that requires verification also reports in `detail` how many findings match it and how many of those are independently verified, and names the agent that must verify the rest (dispatch it)."
  input_schema:
    properties: {}
    type: object
  name: goal.status
- description: "Wait for children you started with `dispatch` and collect their results. Name `handles` (omit them for every child you have not collected yet). Returns each child's status: `done` (with its output and whether it succeeded), `failed`, `abandoned`, or `running` / `pending` if it has not finished within the timeout (join again to keep waiting). `until: any` returns as soon as one of them finishes."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      handles:
        description: "Handles `dispatch` returned; omit for every child of this run not yet joined"
        items:
          type: string
        type: array
      timeout_secs:
        description: "How long to wait, in seconds (0 = just look); default 300"
        maximum: 3600
        minimum: 0
        type: integer
      until:
        description: "Return when all of them have finished (default), or any one"
        enum:
          - all
          - any
        type: string
    type: object
  name: join
- description: "Send a message. `to` is a participant (lynx#1) or its full codename, role:<agent> or step:<id> (every live participant running it), \"parent\", \"lead\", \"operator\", or \"broadcast\" (every participant sees it once, from the moment it started listening; the broadcast log is capped, so don't spam it). Recipients see it before their next model call. Returns the message's `id` and who it reached; `undelivered` says who it didn't, and why."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      body:
        type: string
      to:
        description: "Recipient: a participant, role:<agent>, step:<id>, parent, lead, operator or broadcast"
        type: string
    required:
      - to
      - body
    type: object
  name: msg.send
- description: "Author a NEW workflow for a described task and save it. Returns the saved `file`, the workflow's `name`, its step count and its declared inputs; run it with `dispatch {kind: \"workflow\", file}`. The workflow may only use agents you can dispatch, and it runs unattended (no approval gates, no remote placement)."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      description:
        description: "What the workflow should do, in plain language"
        type: string
    required:
      - description
    type: object
  name: workflows.generate
- description: "Get one workflow's summary by its `id` (the runnable file stem workflows.list shows, not the declared name): description, scope, declared inputs, step count."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      id:
        description: "The workflow's id, as workflows.list shows it"
        type: string
    required:
      - id
    type: object
  name: workflows.get
- description: "List the workflows you can run (global and project). `id` is the runnable identifier (the file stem); `name` is the declared display name. A workflow that failed to parse is listed with its parse_error."
  input_schema:
    properties: {}
    type: object
  name: workflows.list
